# web-f: f folds Svelte, Vue and Astro (#1346). On an `{#each}` line of a Svelte file f folds the
# block to its `{/each}` and f there unfolds it; on its `{:else}` f folds the else branch. The file
# is written here, not in the project, which every other scenario counts the files of.
merl
wait Open a file (fuzzy)
run mkdir -p web && printf '<script>\n  let items = [];\n</script>\n\n<ul>\n  {#each items as item}\n    <li>{item}</li>\n  {:else}\n    <li>No items</li>\n    <li>Add one</li>\n  {/each}\n</ul>\n' > web/List.svelte
key q
wait merl exited: 0
merl web/List.svelte
wait A List.svelte
key :
type 6
key Enter f
wait 5 lines
key f :
type 8
key Enter f
wait 2 lines
key q
wait merl exited: 0
